From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gehrig Wilcox <lougehrig10@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:52:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fix SiLU backward at a short final chunk (channel-first)

When seqlen % (kNThreads * kNElts) < kNElts and seqlen % kNElts != 0 (e.g.
seqlen = 2049), thread 0 bounds-checked the current chunk's index while
loading the tail of the previous chunk, leaving part of it zero. The SiLU
input recomputed at the chunk boundary was then wrong, and so were dx,
dweight and dbias there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 csrc/causal_conv1d_bwd.cu | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/csrc/causal_conv1d_bwd.cu b/csrc/causal_conv1d_bwd.cu
index 917fea3..b0b6ca0 100644
--- a/csrc/causal_conv1d_bwd.cu
+++ b/csrc/causal_conv1d_bwd.cu
@@ -147,7 +147,12 @@ void causal_conv1d_bwd_kernel(ConvParamsBwd params) {
                 } else {
                     #pragma unroll
                     for (int i = 0; i < kNElts; ++i) {
-                        if (chunk * kChunkSize + i < params.seqlen) { x_vals_load[i] = x[-kNElts + i]; }
+                        // These are the last kNElts elements of the *previous* chunk, which are always
+                        // in range when chunk > 0. Bounds-checking the current chunk's index instead
+                        // left them zero when the final chunk has < kNElts valid elements (e.g.
+                        // seqlen = 2049), corrupting the recomputed SiLU input and therefore
+                        // dx / dweight / dbias at that chunk boundary.
+                        if (chunk * kChunkSize - kNElts + i < params.seqlen) { x_vals_load[i] = x[-kNElts + i]; }
                     }
                 }
             }
